
It is useful to divide the main physical parameters and state variables 
associated with a system into several categories:

  - Immutable parameters: These are physical and computational input 
    parameters that are set during initialiation, based on parameters given 
    the parameter file, but that cannot be modified after initialization is 
    completed.

  - Mutable parameters: These are physical input parameters that are 
    required to specify an equilibrium state of a system, but that can be 
    modified by sweep and ramp algorithms.

  - Independent state variables: These are independent variables that may 
    be modified repeatedly either by an SCFT iteration algorithm during the 
    search for a state of minimal free energy or by a stochastic field 
    theoretic simulation algorithm.

  - Dependent state variables: These are variables whose values are computed
    from the parameters and the current state variables.

Immutable parameters:

  - Polymer model (thread or bead model)
  - Number of monomer types
  - Number of polymer species
  - Number of solvent species
  - Polymer topology (number of blocks and connectivity for each species)
  - Ensemble for each species (open or closed)
  - Unit cell lattice system (cubic, orthorhombic, etc.)
  - Space group name (if any)
  - Space group (if any)
  - Mesh dimensions

  The symmetry-adapted basis used in some types of SCFT calculations is also
  an immutable state variable, in a sense, because the set of required basis 
  functions is uniquely determined by a mesh and a space group.

Mutable parameters (modified by sweep and ramp parameters):

  - Kuhn lengths
  - Block lengths (for thread model)
  - Solvent sizes
  - Species volume fractions or chemical potentials
  - Flory-Huggins interaction parameters
  - vMonomer

Independent state variables:

  - W fields for all monomer types [ WFields<D,T> ]
  - Unit cell parameters (edge lengths and angles) 
    [ Domain<D,T>::unitCell ]

Dependent state variables:

  - Data structures maintained by WaveList<D,T> that depend on unit cell
    parameters, including minimalIndices, values for squared wavevectors,
    derivatives o squared wavevectors w/ respect to unit cell parameters,
    etc. 

  - MDE solutions for each block and direction (Propagator<D,T>)

  - Single-molecule partition functions for each species (Polymer<D,T>)

  - Concentration fields for each block (Block<D,T>::cField)

  - Stress contributions for each block (Block<D,T>::stress)

  - Concentration fields for each monomer type (CFields<D,T>::rgrid)

  - Overall stress values (summed over block contributions) (Mixture<D,T>)

  - SCFT free energy and its components (ScftThermo<D,T>)

  - Chi-eigenvector field components maintained by Simulator<D,T>

  - FTS Hamiltonina (Simulator<D,T>)

